Hi @ranma42, I performed further testing and came across an issue with the `TitleCasePipe` (and it might be applicable to some other pipes as well).

Here is a quick example of a pipe, similar to what we have for the `TitleCasePipe` one (from types perspective) in this PR, but a simplified version ([TypeScript playground page](https://www.typescriptlang.org/play?#code/MYGwhgzhAECyCeAFAlgBwKbQN4ChrQBcAnMAOwgDMB7IgWwAoA3MEAV3QC5oJjlSBzAD6lWIEINakAJugp90UgJRceRPkJFiA3HkIly1OkxbsVvAcu7n+O-MTKUaDZm05W1A4aPGSZc0gqWqupeYti6+MgU0Mau0AC88dCaIIrQROgErESkyd62+OmZ2bku7AUAvjhVOMBU5ATQfDxkwJhJAQDucEho6PSKOnUNRRCiBACCEADK1glNDa3oAHT2Bk70AORgAEbAm4PQAPRH0OgAHhjABApcGWMgkzNzABaQ0AAGwQIfhPAYABpoGBrqwWFwvnNBHkxB9avUeKNxlMAHLeebNAhLVb6RxGFKHE5nS7oa63JGPVHot4wD4pX4Ef7oIEgrLgz7ffjQaH0oA)):
```
class SimplePipe {
  transform(value: string|null|undefined): string|null;
  transform(value: string): string;
  transform(value: string|null|undefined): string|null {
    if (value == null) return null;
    return value;
  }
}

const pipe = new SimplePipe();
const result = pipe.transform('abc');
```

What happens here is that the `result` has the `string | null` type, when the expectation is that it should have just `string` (based on the second overload). I believe we should avoid this overlap (so that 2 overloads match the value type) to resolve the issue, so the code of the pipe might look like this ([TypeScript playground page](https://www.typescriptlang.org/play?#)):

```
class SimplePipe {
  transform(value: string): string;
  transform(value: null|undefined): null;
  transform(value: string|null|undefined): string|null {
    if (value == null) return null;
    return value;
  }
}

const pipe = new SimplePipe();
const result = pipe.transform('abc');
```

What do you think?

I'm adding the "blocked" label for now so that we resolve this question before adding this PR to the merge queue.

